/E (The field of natural computing has been the focus of a substantial research effort in recent decades. These bio inspired computing algorithms have proven to be successful problem solvers across domains as varied as management science, telecommunications, business analytics, bioinformatics, finance, marketing, engineering, architecture and design, to name but a few. This course provides a comprehensive introduction to bio inspired computing algorithms. This course requires the student to have a desirable knowledge of Design and Analysis of Algorithms. )
